<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
        {% if debug %}
            <title>Contena Domain Mapping Misconfiguration Help</title>
        {% else %}
            <title>Channel Not Found</title>
        {% endif %}
        <style>
            body {
                font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
                line-height: 1.6;
                color: #333;
                max-width: 1200px;
                margin: 0 auto;
                padding: 20px;
            }

            h1,
            h2 {
                color: #2c3e50;
            }

            .issue {
                background-color: #f8f9fa;
                border-left: 4px solid #007bff;
                padding: 10px;
                margin-bottom: 20px;
            }

            .solution {
                background-color: #e9ecef;
                border-left: 4px solid #28a745;
                padding: 10px;
                margin-top: 10px;
            }

            code {
                white-space: pre;
            }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        {% if not debug %}
            <h1>Channel Not Found</h1>

            <p>Sorry, we could not find a Channel for the current URL. Please check the URL and try again.</p>
            <p>For more information, enable debug mode in <code>.env</code> with <code>APP_DEBUG=1</code>.</p>
        {% endif %}

        {% if debug %}
            <h1>Contena Domain Mapping Misconfiguration Help</h1>

            <p>You accessed Contena with an unknown domain. This page provides guidance on common misconfigurations and how to resolve them.</p>

            <h2>Common Misconfigurations</h2>

            <div class="issue">
                <h3>1. Current URL not matching any Channel domains</h3>
                <p>Known URLs: {% for registeredDomain in registeredDomains %}{{ registeredDomain }}, {% endfor %}</p>
                <div class="solution">
                    <h4>Solution:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Open the Administration.</li>
                        <li>Open the desired Channel under System.</li>
                        <li>Make sure the current URL is configured in its domain settings: <code>{{ domain }}</code></li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="issue">
                <h3>2. Misconfigured proxy header forwarding or trusted proxies</h3>
                <p>Symptoms: Contena cannot resolve a Channel, or assets load with HTTP instead of HTTPS.</p>
                <div class="solution">
                    <h4>Solution:</h4>
                    <p>Make sure the visible browser URL matches the resolved URL: <code>{{ accessedUrl }}</code>.</p>
                    <p>
                        Contena received the following headers from <code>{{ clientIp }}</code>:<br>
                        <code>{{ relevantHeaders|json_encode(constant('JSON_PRETTY_PRINT')) }}</code>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The trusted proxy configuration can look like this:
                    </p>
                    <code>
# config/packages/framework.yaml
framework:
    trusted_proxies: '{{ clientIp }}'
    trusted_headers: [{% for key in trustedProxyRelevantHeaders %} '{{ key }}', {% endfor %}]
                    </code>
                    {% if trustedProxyRelevantHeaders is empty %}
                        <strong>No proxy header was detected. Ensure that the reverse proxy forwards X-Forwarded-For, X-Forwarded-Host and X-Forwarded-Proto.</strong>
                    {% endif %}
                    <p>See the <a href="https://symfony.com/doc/current/deployment/proxies.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Symfony trusted proxies documentation</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </body>
</html>
